PMAT-542 — the PR lane selects the gate the change can move
===========================================================

### 1. the critical path, from the last CI run on main (run 34670955910)
  25.2 min  dogfood            <- the critical path on every code=true PR
   6.3 min  ci / test
   5.8 min  examples-validate
   4.7 min  ci / lint
   4.2 min  ci / coverage
   2.9 min  doctests
   1.2 min  no-default-features
   ... 7 more, each under 0.6 min
  51.8 min  sum of job time
  25.2 min  critical path (the longest job)

  inside dogfood:
   9.0 min  Build the artifact the surface gate measures
   6.2 min  Gate C — surface from the built artifact
   6.1 min  Gate D — documented invocations run against fixtures
   3.8 min  Guard tests        <- the only step a scripts/ or tests/ change can move

### 2. what the two gates actually read
gate C (scripts/dogfood/surface.sh):
  35:CSV="docs/audits/surface_audit.csv"
  plus the built binary. Nothing else — it sources no library.
gate D (scripts/dogfood/docs.sh):
  42:CSV="docs/audits/surface_audit.csv"
  51:COOKBOOK="${COOKBOOK:-${_common_abs}/../forjar-cookbook}"
  82:README = "README.md"
  plus the built binary and the cookbook clone. Nothing else.

